The idea here is that my environment "just works"(TM) if a machine has vim.

`.profile`: drop in $HOME and run `sh -l` to load it.
`.vimrc`: drop in $HOME on any machine that has vim
`.skhdrc`: osx hotkeys to quick navigate common apps

`colors/`: terminal color profiles that I want to keep around

`bin/`: scripts that I keep around

`docs/`: stuff I probably rarely use but when I need it I need it.
